# Rank 1009 / CVE-2026-44643: angular-expressions remote code execution through
# filters. compile("a | __proto__")({}, {}) escapes the expression sandbox: the
# filter name is resolved against JavaScript objects without rejecting
# prototype-sensitive names, and the generated code reaches the Function
# constructor, giving arbitrary code execution (CWE-95, CWE-1321). The fixed
# revision ("Improve security hardening layers", the core of the 1.5.1 ->
# 1.5.2 hardening series) blocks __proto__ property keys, protects the
# Function.prototype.constructor descriptor, and iterates with
# null-prototype contexts -- and its own README update states the hardening is
# not a sandbox and untrusted expressions can still reach code execution.
#
# Detection: the exploitable surface is consumer-side. expressions.compile()
# is documented to turn an expression string into a callable evaluator of the
# same class as the other template and expression compilers
# (Handlebars.compile, ejs.compile, pug.compile, nunjucks.compile,
# lodash.template), so compile's argument is bound as code.TemplateRender
# (VYQL-INJ-008): an expression an attacker controls selects the program the
# evaluator runs, while untrusted scope data only feeds the program's inputs.
# A binding on the library's own AST compiler internals would be repro-shaped,
# answerable only to this CVE's fix layout, and is not how this rank detects.

test "rank1009: compiling an attacker-controlled angular expression is template injection"
  lang javascript
  file consumer.js
  expect VYQL-INJ-008
  code
  ```
  const expressions = require("angular-expressions");

  function render(req, res) {
    const evaluate = expressions.compile(req.query.expr);
    const result = evaluate({}, {});
    res.send(String(result));
  }
  ```

test "rank1009: compiling a fixed expression and only letting scope data vary is safe"
  lang javascript
  file consumer.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-008
  code
  ```
  const expressions = require("angular-expressions");

  function render(req, res) {
    const evaluate = expressions.compile("user.name | uppercase");
    const result = evaluate({ user: req.query.user }, {});
    res.send(String(result));
  }
  ```
